<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">January Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1864</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The January Uprising was a Polish and Lithuanian insurrection against Russian rule, beginning in January 1863 in Congress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Fought mainly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> bands under a secret national government, it was crushed by 1864. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> responded with executions, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportations</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> and the abolition of the kingdom's remaining autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/january-uprising.jpg" alt="January Uprising" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Matejko_-_Polonia_1863_(Poland_Enchained)_-_MNK_XII-453_-_National_Museum_Krak%C3%B3w.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
